WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.701
-Jonathan, welcome.

00:00:02.701 --> 00:00:04.304
Thank you so much
for being here.

00:00:04.304 --> 00:00:08.308
This is your late-night
talk-show debut.

00:00:08.308 --> 00:00:11.177
Just how you always pictured
it happening, over Zoom.

00:00:11.177 --> 00:00:14.747
-Uh, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.
No, it's great, man.

00:00:14.747 --> 00:00:17.316
I mean, I never thought
it would happen, or pictured it.

00:00:17.316 --> 00:00:20.887
But, yeah, it's --
I'm glad to be here, man.

00:00:20.887 --> 00:00:22.321
Very much so.

00:00:22.321 --> 00:00:23.857
-There's so much going on
I want to talk to you about,

00:00:23.857 --> 00:00:25.825
'cause I know
you were in New Mexico

00:00:25.825 --> 00:00:30.563
filming a movie
that is like a Western

00:00:30.563 --> 00:00:32.464
that Jay-Z has produced?
-Yeah.

00:00:32.464 --> 00:00:33.833
-Called "The Harder They Fall."

00:00:33.833 --> 00:00:38.037
And then COVID-19 broke out.
Is that what happened?

00:00:38.037 --> 00:00:41.641
-Yeah, we were a day from --
a day from shooting.

00:00:41.641 --> 00:00:43.309
We had done a pre-shoot day,

00:00:43.309 --> 00:00:45.678
and then we saw the suits
come in

00:00:45.678 --> 00:00:47.880
or the Netflix guys come in,

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:49.982
one-one thousand,
two-one thousand,
three-one thousand.

00:00:49.982 --> 00:00:52.151
They called us all in.

00:00:52.151 --> 00:00:54.487
Which was not the best idea,
when I come and think of it.

00:00:54.487 --> 00:00:56.990
They called us all in one room
to tell us

00:00:56.990 --> 00:00:59.592
that there was a pandemic
and we were shutting down.

00:00:59.592 --> 00:01:01.761
-No, you keep everyone distant.
-But it happened.

00:01:01.761 --> 00:01:03.629
-Yeah.
-Yeah. "Stay where you are.

00:01:03.629 --> 00:01:05.131
Stay where you are
and listen up."

00:01:05.131 --> 00:01:09.636
-Your co-star in "The Harder
They Fall" is Idris Elba,

00:01:09.636 --> 00:01:12.939
a.k.a. one of
The Sexiest Men Alive.

00:01:12.939 --> 00:01:14.507
-Correct, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:14.507 --> 00:01:16.876
Did he hold that
over everyone's head?

00:01:16.876 --> 00:01:20.146
Does he walk around
with a "People" magazine,

00:01:20.146 --> 00:01:21.614
showing everybody?

00:01:21.614 --> 00:01:27.887
-No, the thing about Dris is he
is a very, very, very sweet man.

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:29.555
You know, he's just so gentle.

00:01:29.555 --> 00:01:32.692
And, like, it's almost like --
When you see him, you go,

00:01:32.692 --> 00:01:34.960
"There's no need for you
to tell us that,

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:37.163
because we can see you are
The Sexiest Man Alive."

00:01:37.163 --> 00:01:39.331
-Yeah, yeah, we already know.
-You know, he's like

00:01:39.331 --> 00:01:41.066
"Oh, yeah, of course,
yeah, yeah."

00:01:41.066 --> 00:01:43.035
-I thought you were
going to hold up --

00:01:43.035 --> 00:01:45.271
Because you can show him
that you're coming for him

00:01:45.271 --> 00:01:49.075
because you're on the cover
of October issue of "GQ."

00:01:49.075 --> 00:01:50.843
-Yeah, wow, man.
-I mean, come on!

00:01:50.843 --> 00:01:52.178
-Yeah.
-That's awesome.

00:01:52.178 --> 00:01:53.913
-Yeah, that's all right.
-Congrats, buddy.

00:01:53.913 --> 00:01:55.581
-Thank you, bro. Thank you.

00:01:55.581 --> 00:01:57.550
-Can you think back 20 years ago
when you were a kid?

00:01:57.550 --> 00:02:00.586
Did you ever think one day
you'd be on the cover of "GQ"?

00:02:00.586 --> 00:02:02.621
-You know --
I'll tell you the truth.

00:02:02.621 --> 00:02:04.590
I did think so,
but I thought

00:02:04.590 --> 00:02:06.793
it would be because
I was a basketball star.

00:02:06.793 --> 00:02:08.894
I thought I was
going to be a point guard.

00:02:08.894 --> 00:02:10.563
-Really?
-Playing in the NBA, yeah.

00:02:10.563 --> 00:02:12.231
That was like --
That was, like, the plan.

00:02:12.231 --> 00:02:15.901
And then my uncle,

00:02:15.901 --> 00:02:20.672
who is probably
my closest mentor to this day --

00:02:20.672 --> 00:02:21.974
I was about 14 years old.

00:02:21.974 --> 00:02:24.944
I was playing ball.
And he came to the game, man.

00:02:24.944 --> 00:02:27.647
I was like, "Okay, Uncle Chuck's
coming to the game.

00:02:27.647 --> 00:02:29.115
I got to clown.
I got to do my thing."

00:02:29.115 --> 00:02:30.616
And I played my ass off, man.

00:02:30.616 --> 00:02:34.120
And at the end of the game,
he pulled me to the side.

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:35.487
I was in his truck.

00:02:35.487 --> 00:02:37.523
And he said, "Nephew,
I got something to tell you."

00:02:37.523 --> 00:02:39.792
I'm like, "what? Tell me.
What was it? What was it?

00:02:39.792 --> 00:02:41.427
What'd you like?
What'd you like?"

00:02:41.427 --> 00:02:43.996
He said, "I don't think
this basketball thing

00:02:43.996 --> 00:02:45.331
is going to work out.

00:02:45.331 --> 00:02:46.866
-Aww.
-I don't think it's for you."

00:02:46.866 --> 00:02:49.234
-No.
-And I go -- Yeah.

00:02:49.234 --> 00:02:51.404
I go -- I go, "What?"

00:02:51.404 --> 00:02:54.373
We didn't talk for probably --
probably six months.

00:02:54.373 --> 00:02:55.975
I didn't talk to my uncle.

00:02:55.975 --> 00:02:58.243
And, mind you, I'm 6 feet tall.

00:02:58.243 --> 00:03:01.547
My uncle's about 6'5"

00:03:01.547 --> 00:03:05.017
and just a brilliant athlete.

00:03:05.017 --> 00:03:07.119
-So he knows how to play.

00:03:07.119 --> 00:03:09.054
-And so he says it.
I go, "Okay, cool."

00:03:09.054 --> 00:03:11.457
And then that kind of put me
on the track, though.

00:03:11.457 --> 00:03:13.893
You know, that's a hard no.
You know?

00:03:13.893 --> 00:03:15.695
-I would have --
I would have started

00:03:15.695 --> 00:03:17.230
to break down crying
right there.

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:19.165
I would have been like --
-Oh, that happened.

00:03:19.165 --> 00:03:21.100
That absolutely happened.
In his Chevrolet.

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:23.936
In his white Chevrolet truck.
-Wow.

00:03:23.936 --> 00:03:27.339
And then you thought, "Oh,
acting is what I want to do."

00:03:27.339 --> 00:03:30.876
-I was --
I was kind of already in it.

00:03:30.876 --> 00:03:33.246
I was kind of already --

00:03:33.246 --> 00:03:35.814
Things had happened in school,
you know,

00:03:35.814 --> 00:03:38.585
trouble and all that stuff,
and kind of put me on that path,

00:03:38.585 --> 00:03:41.153
and I was getting into it
at that point.

00:03:41.153 --> 00:03:43.656
But then -- It was
kind of like a turbo boost

00:03:43.656 --> 00:03:45.958
when Uncle Chuck was like,
"Nah, nephew."

00:03:45.958 --> 00:03:47.393
You know.
And it was so sober.

00:03:47.393 --> 00:03:48.995
That's the thing.
It was so sober.

00:03:48.995 --> 00:03:50.729
I was like, "Okay."
-Wow.

00:03:50.729 --> 00:03:53.066
-"All right, then."
-Wow, that was --

00:03:53.066 --> 00:03:54.767
Yeah. "You really said that."
Oh, my gosh.

00:03:54.767 --> 00:03:56.936
"You didn't break it down
like I'm a little kid.

00:03:56.936 --> 00:03:58.938
You're like,
'It's over, dude, yeah.'"

00:03:58.938 --> 00:04:01.340
-"It's not for you."
That's exactly what he said.

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:03.309
"It's not for you."
And I said, "Okay."

00:04:03.309 --> 00:04:04.644
-Wow.
-Yeah.

00:04:04.644 --> 00:04:07.079
-Actually worked out.
It worked out, man.

00:04:07.079 --> 00:04:08.347
Wow. I mean --

00:04:08.347 --> 00:04:11.751
-We still got on the cover
of "GQ," Uncle Chuck.

00:04:11.751 --> 00:04:12.818
It still happened.

00:04:12.818 --> 00:04:14.854
-It still happened.
You can't stop --

00:04:14.854 --> 00:04:16.422
You can't stop a train, yeah.

00:04:16.422 --> 00:04:17.856
No, no, no.
-Yeah.

00:04:17.856 --> 00:04:19.158
-I want to talk about

00:04:19.158 --> 00:04:21.460
"Lovecraft Country."
-Definitely.

00:04:21.460 --> 00:04:24.530
-But first, there's a rumor out
there I want to ask you about.

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:27.366
It was reported,
I think it was last week,

00:04:27.366 --> 00:04:30.435
that you might be joining
the Marvel cinematic universe

00:04:30.435 --> 00:04:33.806
as Kang the Conqueror.

00:04:33.806 --> 00:04:35.808
Now, you'd tell me
if this is true, right?

00:04:35.808 --> 00:04:38.811
There's no one here
in the studio. It's just us.

00:04:38.811 --> 00:04:42.147
-It's just you and me?
-Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:04:42.147 --> 00:04:44.550
-Man, I heard
the same thing, bro.

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:45.851
I heard the same thing.

00:04:45.851 --> 00:04:48.720
It was like,
"What? What? What?"

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:51.223
So -- You know.

00:04:51.223 --> 00:04:54.026
We -- We apparently
have the same source

00:04:54.026 --> 00:04:55.862
because I heard it, too.

00:04:55.862 --> 00:05:00.399
-God. I knew -- I knew
I was gonna get nothing.

00:05:00.399 --> 00:05:02.568
Let's talk about
"Lovecraft Country."

00:05:02.568 --> 00:05:04.737
It's a big hit. Oh, my gosh.
Congrats on this.

00:05:04.737 --> 00:05:06.872
All my writers love it.
Everyone's like,

00:05:06.872 --> 00:05:09.341
"That's the show you've
got to watch right now."

00:05:09.341 --> 00:05:12.445
For anyone who hasn't seen it,
how would you describe it?

00:05:12.445 --> 00:05:15.748
-It's a story about a family

00:05:15.748 --> 00:05:19.185
and a man searching

00:05:19.185 --> 00:05:22.321
for their legacy

00:05:22.321 --> 00:05:25.925
during a very turbulent time
in America.

00:05:25.925 --> 00:05:31.797
Right? It takes place
during the Jim Crow era.

00:05:31.797 --> 00:05:35.802
And they move through
this America

00:05:35.802 --> 00:05:40.406
as Black people
attempting to stay safe,

00:05:40.406 --> 00:05:45.310
to grow as a family,
and to push the lineage forward.

00:05:45.310 --> 00:05:49.515
And chaos ensues
on so many levels,

00:05:49.515 --> 00:05:51.383
you couldn't even imagine.

00:05:51.383 --> 00:05:53.218
-You're great in this.

00:05:53.218 --> 00:05:55.221
As we said, the show
takes place in the '50s,

00:05:55.221 --> 00:05:57.956
but there are a lot of themes,
I would say,

00:05:57.956 --> 00:06:00.726
in "Lovecraft Country"
that feel relevant now.

00:06:00.726 --> 00:06:02.861
-Yeah.
-Especially given the news

00:06:02.861 --> 00:06:06.532
yesterday of the Breonna Taylor
grand-jury decision.

00:06:06.532 --> 00:06:09.335
Does it feel even more special
to be part of this show

00:06:09.335 --> 00:06:11.471
where we are right now?

00:06:11.471 --> 00:06:13.505
-Um...

00:06:13.505 --> 00:06:16.008
You know, that's a --
that's a tough word, isn't it?

00:06:16.008 --> 00:06:18.111
"Special." You know?

00:06:18.111 --> 00:06:20.179
-Yeah.
-Like, it's --

00:06:20.179 --> 00:06:22.514
But it does. It feels novel.

00:06:22.514 --> 00:06:27.152
It feels --
There's a certain gravity to it.

00:06:27.152 --> 00:06:29.154
I wouldn't say weight.
I'd say gravity to it.

00:06:29.154 --> 00:06:30.555
You know what I mean?

00:06:30.555 --> 00:06:35.794
And you know, with Sister
Taylor, it's heavy. You know?

00:06:35.794 --> 00:06:39.131
'Cause you look at our show,
and kind of what I feel

00:06:39.131 --> 00:06:41.066
we've done
is a lot of folks say,

00:06:41.066 --> 00:06:42.968
"Oh, it's so relevant."
You know?

00:06:42.968 --> 00:06:45.437
I say, "Yeah -- I mean,
most things are relevant."

00:06:45.437 --> 00:06:46.705
You know what I'm saying?

00:06:46.705 --> 00:06:48.240
Like, everybody's
in charge of making it.

00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:51.510
You know what I'm saying?
But nobody's a fool, you know?

00:06:51.510 --> 00:06:53.879
But to make something
that is both relevant

00:06:53.879 --> 00:06:58.117
and, in my opinion,
revealing, is a bit of a --

00:06:58.117 --> 00:06:59.652
bit of a hat trick, you know?

00:06:59.652 --> 00:07:02.021
Because what the show does --
One of the things

00:07:02.021 --> 00:07:04.123
I've said before,
and I'll say it again,

00:07:04.123 --> 00:07:09.395
it's like you put a body cam
on an entire culture, you know?

00:07:09.395 --> 00:07:14.400
And the advent of the body cam
really blew everybody's mind.

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:16.402
Like, "Ooh, my God, I can't
believe this [bleep] happening

00:07:16.402 --> 00:07:18.871
to so-and-so at these stops."

00:07:18.871 --> 00:07:21.440
But to put a body cam
on an entire culture

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:26.278
for just a day in the life
is such a --

00:07:26.278 --> 00:07:28.681
It's such a special thing,
as you say, you know.

00:07:28.681 --> 00:07:30.683
And those body cams,
we're putting them

00:07:30.683 --> 00:07:33.185
on our Black bodies, you know.

00:07:33.185 --> 00:07:37.256
And we're telling something
that allegedly was in the past,

00:07:37.256 --> 00:07:39.658
but as we can see,

00:07:39.658 --> 00:07:43.662
with Sister Taylor,
is very current, you know?

00:07:43.662 --> 00:07:47.533
And we reveal that,
you know, every Sunday.

00:07:47.533 --> 00:07:49.868
So, yeah, "special"
is an interesting word.

00:07:49.868 --> 00:07:51.237
And I would say
that's what it is.

00:07:51.237 --> 00:07:53.538
-I want to show everyone a clip.

00:07:53.538 --> 00:07:56.275
Here's Jonathan Majors
in "Lovecraft Country."

00:07:56.275 --> 00:07:58.010
Take a look at this.

00:07:58.010 --> 00:08:03.115
♪♪

00:08:03.115 --> 00:08:05.685
-Her name was Young-ja.
She's was a nurse.

00:08:05.685 --> 00:08:07.719
Your unit shot some of us
at checkpoint

00:08:07.719 --> 00:08:10.823
then dragged her away!

00:08:10.823 --> 00:08:12.725
-She was a communist
sympathizer.

00:08:12.725 --> 00:08:15.694
-Is that what you tell yourself?
-I was following orders.

00:08:15.694 --> 00:08:17.129
Who knows how many lives
I've saved by doing what I did?

00:08:17.129 --> 00:08:18.998
-Does it have balance,
how many have you taken?

00:08:18.998 --> 00:08:21.967
The ones that keep you
up at night and sobbing?

00:08:21.967 --> 00:08:25.705
There's no book for you
to escape what you have done.

00:08:25.705 --> 00:08:28.840
-You knew this entire time
but didn't say a word?

00:08:28.840 --> 00:08:32.377
Ji, you made me care for you?
What's wrong with you?

00:08:32.377 --> 00:08:34.980
-Nothing is wrong with me.

00:08:34.980 --> 00:08:37.849
You're the monster!

00:08:37.849 --> 00:08:39.385
-Why did you agree
to go out with me, then?!

00:08:39.385 --> 00:08:42.822
-Because I was
going to kill you.

00:08:42.822 --> 00:08:44.456
-Jonathan Majors, everybody.

00:08:44.456 --> 00:08:47.526
Check out "Lovecraft Country"
Sundays at 9:00 p.m.

00:08:47.526 --> 00:08:51.030
on HBO and streaming on HBO Max.

00:08:51.030 --> 00:08:53.866
And he's on the cover,
come on, of "GQ."

00:08:53.866 --> 00:08:56.402
Hear that, Uncle Chuck?
We'll be right back.

